<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="55.1" level="1">Property and Conveyances</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="IV" level="2">Common Interest Communities</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="19" level="3">Virginia Condominium Act</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="3" level="4">Management of Condominium</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>55.1-1946</section_number>
	<catch_line>Management office</catch_line>
	<text>
		Unless the condominium instruments expressly provide otherwise, the unit owners' association shall not be prohibited from maintaining a management office on common elements or in one or more units in the condominium.
	</text>
	<history>1982, c. 545, § 55-79.74:2; 2019, c. 712.</history>
</law>
